1
00:05:53,333 --> 00:05:59,333
A Doll's House is a drama film directed by Joseph Losey.

2
00:11:46,666 --> 00:11:52,666
Nora Helmer lives a quiet life with her husband,
Torvald, in a small Norwegian town.

3
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:46,000
While he works diligently at a bank, she looks after their children.

4
00:23:33,333 --> 00:23:39,333
But Torvald doesn't know that several years ago, when he was very ill and she was desperate for money,
Nora forged a loan document and has been secretly working to pay the money back ever since.

5
00:29:26,666 --> 00:29:32,666
The arrival of her friend Kristine prompts Nora to
re-evaluate her life and confront Torvald.

6
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:26,000
Nora Helmer, played by Jane Fonda.

7
00:41:13,333 --> 00:41:19,333
Nils Krogstad, played by Edward Fox.

8
00:47:06,666 --> 00:47:12,666
Dr. Rank, played by Trevor Howard.

9
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
Kristine Linde, played by Delphine Seyrig.

10
00:58:53,333 --> 00:58:59,333
Torvald Helmer, played by David Warner.

11
01:04:46,666 --> 01:04:52,666
Olssen, played by Pierre Oudrey.

12
01:10:40,000 --> 01:10:46,000
A Doll's House is a 1973 drama film directed by Joseph Losey, based
on the 1879 play A Doll's House by Henrik Ibsen.

13
01:16:33,333 --> 01:16:39,333
It stars Jane Fonda in the role of Nora Helmer and David
Warner as her domineering husband, Torvald.

14
01:22:26,666 --> 01:22:32,666
Losey's version of the play was extensively adapted for film.

15
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:26,000
From Ibsen's expository dialogue, entire new scenes were developed by British
dramatist David Mercer and integrated through a number of invented sets.

16
01:34:13,333 --> 01:34:19,333
The film explores themes of friendship, feminism, based on
play or musical, friends, women's rights.

17
01:40:06,666 --> 01:40:12,666
The tone is emotional.
